WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.575
Some lights have colored sectors.

2
00:00:02.825 --> 00:00:13.675
A red sector usually covers a hazard, such as a shoal or reef, so if you see the light turn red, you’re standing into danger and should move back into the white sector.

3
00:00:13.925 --> 00:00:21.675
The Light List gives sector boundaries in degrees true, as seen from a vessel looking toward the light, not from the light outward.

4
00:00:21.925 --> 00:00:24.200
That’s a common exam trap.

5
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:34.825
You can also use the moment a light first appears over the horizon, called bobbing a light, to estimate your distance off by comparing it with the geographic range.
